      <!-- Section: Data Set -->
      
        <div id="dataSet" class="section metadataSection">
          <div class="section__header sh">
  <h2 class="sh__main" id="headerDataSetInformation">Data Set Information</h2>
  
  
  
  
  

</div>
          <div class="section__content">
            
            
              
  

              <table class="name-value-table" aria-labelledby="headerDataSetInformation">
                
  <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Data Set Scope Code:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">Data Set</td>
</tr>
  <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Data Set Type:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">GIS shapefile</td>
</tr>
  <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Maintenance Frequency:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">Continually</td>
</tr>
  <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Maintenance Note:
  </th>
  <td class="small">
    
  <p>Updates to the digital U.S. maritime limits and boundaries are primarily triggered by geographical changes or new international agreements. These geographical changes include significant accretion or erosion of the charted low water line (approximately 500 meters or more), or alterations to low tide elevations (like rocks awash) based on new hydrographic survey information. New treaties or international agreements with neighboring coastal states can also necessitate updates.</p>

  </td>
</tr>
  <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Data Presentation Form:
  </th>
  <td class="ellipsisize">Vector digital data</td>
</tr>
  
  
  
  <tr>
  <th scope="col">
    Distribution Liability:
  </th>
  <td class="small">
    
  <p>Users must assume responsibility to determine the appropriate use of this data set. The digital maritime limits are not to be used for a legal definition. The legal definition still remains the depiction on NOAA&#39;s nautical charts.</p>

  </td>
</tr>
  

              </table>
            
          </div>
        </div><!-- .section Data Set -->
      

